  "result": "The change looks clean and minimal in scope. Summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed `-X`/`--exec-batch` failing with \"Argument list too long\" when passed a very large number of files.\n\n**Root cause:** `generate_and_execute_batch` in `src/exec/mod.rs` built a single `Command` with every matched path appended as an argument, with no bound on the total argument-list size, so on large result sets it exceeded the OS's `ARG_MAX`.\n\n**Fix:** The batch executor now splits the paths into multiple chunks sized to stay under the platform's actual argument-length limit (queried via `sysconf(_SC_ARG_MAX)` on Unix, with a conservative fallback elsewhere and a safety margin reserved for the environment), running the command once per chunk and merging the exit codes (`src/exec/mod.rs`).\n\n**Verification:**\n- `cargo build` succeeds.\n- `cargo test --bin fd exec` \u2014 all 24 existing exec-related tests pass unchanged.\n- Manual repro: created 300,000 files and ran `fd -IH . -tf -X wc -l`, which previously failed with \"Argument list too long\"; it now completes successfully across multiple batched invocations.\n\nNo tests, docs, or config were modified.",
